# Turn SW1 (Service Mode) on AFTER the game has booted, rather than at power-up.
#
# RESULT: this does NOT reach the settings menu. It hits the same IO ERROR 64,
# roughly 600 frames later than the power-up path. Toggling the DIP mid-run
# evidently re-enters the boot sequence, so it meets the same C040 timeout
# (tri-RAM offset 0 must read 0xA6 within ~0.65s) and falls into the self-test.
# Matches the behaviour reported on MiSTer hardware.
#
# Verified with FRAMES=1900: the late burst at 1311..1339 has byte-identical
# frame sizes and deltas to the power-up error burst at 681..709. A shorter run
# stops around frame 789 and looks like it succeeded - it has not, so do not
# judge this script with FRAMES below ~1500.
#
#   FRAMES=1900 ROMS_HOST=~/mameroms ./sim-core.sh shouse blastoff \
#       ../blastoff/service.cab
#
# Kept because it documents that there is currently no route into the menu:
# neither a warm reset (see warmreset.cab) nor a mid-run DIP toggle works.

# 1. boot to attract with SW1 off
500

# 2. SW1 on
1200 dipsw=fffe
